{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>If I have sharpened.</b> Even though I sharpened the flash of My sword against Israel in the days of the destruction — it was not the mouth of My sword." "<b>And it takes hold of the judgment of My hand.</b> And even though afterward it takes hold of the judgment of My hand against them, for יָדִין ה׳ עַמּוֹ — nevertheless." "<b>I will render vengeance to My adversaries.</b> The vengeance that the nations wrought upon Israel, as it says: יַעַן עֲשׂוֹת אֱדוֹם בִּנְקֹם נָקָם לְבֵית יְהוּדָה (Ezekiel 25:12) — I will repay that vengeance upon them, as it says: וְנָתַתִּי נִקְמָתִי בֶּאֱדוֹם בְּיַד עַמִּי יִשְׂרָאֵל (Ezekiel 25:14)." "<b>And I will recompense those who hate Me.</b> Recompense measure for measure, as it says: כַּאֲשֶׁר עָשִׂיתָ כֵּן יֵעָשֶׂה לָּךְ, גְּמֻלְךָ יָשׁוּב בְּרֹאשֶׁךָ (Obadiah 1:15)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:28.188000480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}